    {
      "id": "p0203-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In 1994, Square released Final Fantasy VI for the Japanese Super Famicom and the North American Super NES. As another of Square's classic Japanese RPGs, Final Fantasy VI combined established game design with entertaining innovations and surprises. Like many of Square's games from the 1990s, Final Fantasy VI enjoyed great critical success and inspired a new generation of game designers.",
        "raw": "In 1994, Square released Final Fantasy VI for the Japanese Super Famicom\nand the North American Super NES. As another of Square's classic\nJapanese RPGs, Final Fantasy VI combined established game design\nwith entertaining innovations and surprises. Like many of Square's\ngames from the 1990s, Final Fantasy VI enjoyed great critical success and\ninspired a new generation of game designers.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
